    },
    {
      "locator": "COMMENTS (C.11), zero clause",
      "source_quote": "T(n, prime(pi(n)+1)) = 0 for n >= 5",
      "status": "proved",
      "proof": "Corollary 4",
      "statement": "T(n,q)=0 for every n>=1 and prime q>n",
      "registered_problem_id": null
    },
    {
      "locator": "COMMENTS (C.11), first-zero clause",
      "source_quote": "the first zero in row n, T(n,k) = 0, appears to occur at k equal to the next prime after n for n >= 5. Thus, T(5,7) = 0, T(6,7) = 0, T(7,11) = 0, T(8,11) = 0, T(11,13) = 0, T(13,17) = 0, etc.",
      "status": "open in this note",
      "evidence": "Finite checks for rows 5 through 79",
      "registered_problem_id": null
    },
    {
      "locator": "FORMULA (1)",
      "source_quote": "Sum_{k=0..floor((n+1)/2)^2} T(n,k) * x^(-k) equals the power series expansion of Sum_{k=-oo..oo} x^k * (1 - x^k)^(n+k) after being truncated to include only nonpositive powers of x, for n >= 1 (by definition).",
      "status": "definition with support proved",
      "proof": "Definition (1) and Lemma 1",
      "registered_problem_id": null
    },
    {
      "locator": "FORMULA (2)",
      "source_quote": "Sum_{k=0..floor((n+1)/2)^2} T(n,k) = 0 for n >= 1 (conjecture).",
      "status": "proved",
      "proof": "Corollary 5",
      "registered_problem_id": "oeis-a391810-full-laurent-row-sums"
    },
    {
      "locator": "FORMULA (3)",
      "source_quote": "Sum_{k=0..floor((n+1)/2)^2} k * T(n,k) = 1 for n >= 1 (conjecture).",
      "status": "proved",
      "proof": "Corollary 5",
      "registered_problem_id": "oeis-a391810-laurent-first-moment"
    },
    {
      "locator": "FORMULA (4)",
      "source_quote": "Sum_{k=0..floor((n+1)/2)^2} k^2 * T(n,k) = -(2*n-5) for n >= 2 (conjecture).",
      "status": "proved",
      "proof": "Corollary 5",
      "registered_problem_id": "oeis-a391810-second-moment"
    },
    {
      "locator": "FORMULA (5)",
      "source_quote": "Sum_{k=0..floor((n+1)/2)^2} -(-1)^k * T(n,k) = 2*round(2^n/3) = 2*A001045(n) for n >= 1 (conjecture), where A001045 is the Jacobsthal numbers (g.f. x/((1+x)*(1-2*x))).",
      "status": "proved",
      "proof": "Theorem 1",
      "registered_problem_id": "oeis-a391810-alternating-jacobsthal"
    },
    {
      "locator": "FORMULA (6)",
      "source_quote": "Sum_{k=0..floor((n+1)/2)^2} -(-1)^k * k * T(n,k), n >= 1, forms a sequence with g.f. x*(1-x+8*x^2)/((1+x)^2*(1-2*x)^2) (conjecture), and begins [1, 1, 13, 25, 81, 181, 453, 1025, ...].",
      "status": "proved",
      "proof": "Corollary 6",
      "registered_problem_id": null
    },
    {
      "locator": "FORMULA (7)",
      "source_quote": "Sum_{k=0..floor((n+1)/2)^2} T(n,k)^2 = 2*A391811(n) for n >= 1.",
      "status": "defining relation with positive integrality proved",
      "proof": "Squared-norm paragraph after Corollary 6",
      "registered_problem_id": null
    },
    {
